{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Where to Perform Data Validation?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you are discussing about data validation. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Designs the data structure based on the database structures and its characteristics.  Validate database using the proper IT tools."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Exchanges simple information on the data validation and data warehouses."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<strong>Present Perfect Versus Past Simple- Affirmative Form</strong>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>The <strong>Present Perfect</strong> as well as the <strong>Past Simple</strong> refer to two different moments in time.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Boss, I think you may want to check what I have done since last Monday when I started teleworking. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p><strong>PRESENT PERFECT</strong></p> <p>You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense to talk about an action or situation that started in the past but continue up to the present moment (unfinished actions). Remember that the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense needs the auxiliary verb &ldquo;have&rdquo; or &ldquo;has&rdquo; plus the past participle form of the verb.</p></br>Example:</br><span class=\"italic\">Check what I <span class=\"strong\">have done</span> since last Monday.</span></br></br> <p><strong>PAST SIMPLE</strong></p> <p>You use the <span class=\"strong\">past simple</span> tense to talk about an action or situation that took place in the past (finished actions). Remember that, depending on the type of the verb, regular or irregular, the verb will change differently to its <span class=\"strong\">simple past</span> form.</p></br>Example:</br> <span class=\"italic\">Last week I <span class=\"strong\">worked</span> from home so I'd better report to my boss what I <span class=\"strong\">did</span></span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I decided to carry out two different techniques I have mastered throughout my work here."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<strong>Data Validation Techniques</strong>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are different techniques that help us validate data in big projects and avoid errors as much as possible. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p><strong>RANGE VALIDATION </strong></p> <p>This technique applies only to dates and numbers. A test is performed in order to confirm that the registered values are in specific minimum and maximum ranges.&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>LOOKUP VALIDATION </strong></p> <p>This validation technique is performed when the registered data has to be contrasted with other possible values or data. A comparison is performed in order to state whether the entries are valid or not.<strong>&nbsp;</strong></p> <p><strong>MASKED INPUT VALIDATION</strong></p> <p>There are some data or values that require a specific input pattern to be registered in the databases. Therefore, this technique, also known as Filtered Input Validation, only allows to register specific data that follows a pre-established pattern or data type. This is useful when pieces of information such as dates, telephone numbers, among others. </p>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "telework "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "working from home using the computer"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Boss, I think you may want to check what I have done since last Monday when I started teleworking."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "current "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "actual, in the present moment"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've studied the parts where data validation ought to be performed in our current project."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "susceptible "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "easy to influence or occur"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I identified all the different parts of the application that required interaction from the user as those were the ones that were more susceptible to suffer from human mistakes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "master "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to reach a high level of knowledge and skill"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I decided to carry out two different techniques I have mastered throughout my work here."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "range "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a group of values"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: First, I used the range validation technique which I applied to the numbers and dates in order to confirm that the registered values were within the specific minimum and maximum ranges."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "array "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to show or portray"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Plus, you ought to make sure that telephone numbers and dates were correctly arrayed with their respective patterns.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob09aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about data validation techniques."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write notes about how you apply them into a system development."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a presentation in order to explain the different techniques."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with your classmate and answer all his questions. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for information about data validation techniques."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write notes about how you apply them into a system development."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about the application of different validation techniques."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n5le02ob09re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n5le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Thomas</strong>: Last week I worked from home so I&rsquo;d better report to my boss what I did. Here she comes. Boss, I think you might want to check what I have done since last Monday when I started teleworking.<br /><strong>Susan</strong>: Sure, show me that.<br /><strong>Thomas</strong>: I&rsquo;ve studied the parts where data validation ought to be performed in our current project. Therefore, I started with the user interactivity screens and forms. So, I identified all the different parts of the application that required interaction from the users, as those who were more susceptible to suffer from human mistakes. Then, I continued with the file manipulation routines which were basically the parts in which reading and writing operations from and to the file were involved."}, {"time": "48400", "image": "enpe8n5le02ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Susan</strong>: Correct. &nbsp;Remember that you ought to include the import and export routines too in which customers might want to save data in different file formats for other types of systems. Now, what techniques did you use?<br /><strong>Thomas</strong>: I decided to carry out two different techniques I have mastered throughout my work here. First, I used the range validation technique which I applied to the numbers and dates in order to confirm that the registered values were within the specific minimum and maximum ranges. Then, I proceeded with the lookup validation in which I contrasted the data with other possible values and data just to make sure that they were valid."}, {"time": "93000", "image": "enpe8n5le02ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Susan</strong>: You&rsquo;d better use the masked input validation, right? It is important that you pay attention to those values in which specific input patterns have to be included. Plus, you ought to make sure that telephone numbers and dates were correctly arrayed with their respective patterns.&nbsp; If you have any questions, you may want to call me at the office."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n5le02ob09re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about where data validation was performed in a system."}, {"type": "Lea